00:13:43.100 --> 00:13:44.870
and you're nervous and you're not swimming well,

302
00:13:44.870 --> 00:13:46.270
and your walls are awful,

303
00:13:46.270 --> 00:13:48.680
and you're just like chopping through the water.

304
00:13:48.680 --> 00:13:49.513
And then it's like,

305
00:13:49.513 --> 00:13:52.060
"What am I making such a big deal out of this?"

306
00:13:52.060 --> 00:13:57.060
And then slowly you return into what you're capable of.

307
00:13:58.090 --> 00:14:01.830
And that's the hardest part, that dichotomy.

308
00:14:01.830 --> 00:14:05.640
Caring enough for the result and the outcome,

309
00:14:05.640 --> 00:14:07.310
but also letting go enough

310
00:14:07.310 --> 00:14:11.450
for letting the result and outcome to happen for you.

311
00:14:11.450 --> 00:14:12.490
The Eckhart Tolle.

312
00:14:12.490 --> 00:14:14.963
Yeah, hat's literally my favorite.

313
00:14:15.940 --> 00:14:19.180
Right now I'm living in a space of possibilities

314
00:14:19.180 --> 00:14:22.330
on both sides of everything, like both things can be true.

315
00:14:22.330 --> 00:14:27.330
And I don't work with older athletes like you do,

316
00:14:27.380 --> 00:14:29.570
but the younger generation, these teenagers,

317
00:14:29.570 --> 00:14:30.480
it's the same thing.

318
00:14:30.480 --> 00:14:34.060
It's like this I don't want to let go of that control

319
00:14:34.060 --> 00:14:35.430
because if I let go of that control,

320
00:14:35.430 --> 00:14:37.540
then I'm gonna fail.

321
00:14:37.540 --> 00:14:42.020
I have, then my confidence will go down the drain.

322
00:14:42.020 --> 00:14:42.920
All of these other things

323
00:14:42.920 --> 00:14:44.780
that people just hold on so tightly to,

324
00:14:44.780 --> 00:14:46.560
and to let go

325
00:14:46.560 --> 00:14:50.210
is such a physical experience too

326
00:14:50.210 --> 00:14:52.290
that you have to experience through your body,

327
00:14:52.290 --> 00:14:55.290
which I'm a big fan of just that whole conversation.

328
00:14:55.290 --> 00:14:57.644
But I think we try to use our minds

329
00:14:57.644 --> 00:15:00.020
to wrap around that

330
00:15:00.020 --> 00:15:02.140
to where it's like, I'm just gonna let go with my mind.

331
00:15:02.140 --> 00:15:03.900
And then yes, we can let go with our minds

332
00:15:03.900 --> 00:15:06.113
but then we're just, our bodies are still tense

333
00:15:06.113 --> 00:15:07.680
and our minds are trying to let go

334
00:15:07.680 --> 00:15:08.900
and conceptualize this thing

335
00:15:08.900 --> 00:15:10.230
that we haven't actually experienced

336
00:15:10.230 --> 00:15:12.100
through our whole physical being,

337
00:15:12.100 --> 00:15:14.350
which I think quarantine has allowed people

338
00:15:14.350 --> 00:15:17.070
to tap in to themselves in a different way,

339
00:15:17.070 --> 00:15:18.880
because they don't have that physical outlet

340
00:15:18.880 --> 00:15:20.670
in the same way

341
00:15:20.670 --> 00:15:24.660
so they have to release physically through other modalities.

342
00:15:24.660 --> 00:15:28.400
I think that that's an appropriate kinda place

343
00:15:28.400 --> 00:15:30.130
to segue into something you were talking about

344
00:15:30.130 --> 00:15:31.460
in your podcast the other day,

345
00:15:31.460 --> 00:15:34.300
which is this idea, well, two ideas,

346
00:15:34.300 --> 00:15:35.140
the first being

347
00:15:37.990 --> 00:15:40.230
to think about not just working out,

348
00:15:40.230 --> 00:15:41.360
but working in,

349
00:15:41.360 --> 00:15:43.210
which is kind of what we've already been talking about.

350
00:15:43.210 --> 00:15:47.130
But also this idea of showing up is not enough.

351
00:15:47.130 --> 00:15:50.390
Like where is the intentionality that you're bringing

352
00:15:50.390 --> 00:15:51.850
to what it is that you're doing?

353
00:15:51.850 --> 00:15:53.700
And of course this is something that's applicable

354
00:15:53.700 --> 00:15:56.210
to any athlete, how they're approaching

355
00:15:56.210 --> 00:15:57.830
their training regimen,

356
00:15:57.830 --> 00:16:00.760
but in life to whatever it is that we're doing,

357
00:16:00.760 --> 00:16:04.210
particularly now where everything has been upended

358
00:16:04.210 --> 00:16:06.470
and it's causing confusion and anxiety,

359
00:16:06.470 --> 00:16:08.670
and we're all kind of asking ourselves questions

360
00:16:08.670 --> 00:16:10.330
about like, "Why am I doing this?"

361
00:16:10.330 --> 00:16:12.980
Yeah.
Like we're all being-

362
00:16:12.980 --> 00:16:14.100
Reevaluating, yeah.
Yeah, we're all,

363
00:16:14.100 --> 00:16:17.550
everybody's re-evaluating in their own way right now.

364
00:16:17.550 --> 00:16:19.887
Yeah, but that's part of what I go into there.

365
00:16:19.887 --> 00:16:23.210
And that is once you have your purpose and your clarity,

366
00:16:23.210 --> 00:16:25.269
you can show up with intention

367
00:16:25.269 --> 00:16:27.520
because you're not questioning the goals.

368
00:16:27.520 --> 00:16:28.493
You're not questioning the path.

369
00:16:28.493 --> 00:16:31.230
Now you can focus all your attention

370
00:16:31.230 --> 00:16:33.970
onto executing the next workout,

371
00:16:33.970 --> 00:16:37.280
the next day at work, this project

372
00:16:37.280 --> 00:16:38.660
to the best of your ability,

373
00:16:38.660 --> 00:16:40.470
'cause you're not wondering, well, why am I,

374
00:16:40.470 --> 00:16:42.527
you don't wanna be asking, why am I doing this?

375
00:16:42.527 --> 00:16:45.750
'Cause that takes everything that you have

376
00:16:45.750 --> 00:16:47.840
in that workout or in that project

377
00:16:47.840 --> 00:16:50.410
or that vacation with your family,

378
00:16:50.410 --> 00:16:52.370
you show up with intention too.

379
00:16:52.370 --> 00:16:54.800
Like, if you start wondering, why am I here,

380
00:16:54.800 --> 00:16:56.810
you're not gonna have a good vacation.

381
00:16:56.810 --> 00:16:57.940
You're not gonna have a good workout.

382
00:16:57.940 --> 00:17:01.480
You're not gonna have a good work outcome.

383
00:17:01.480 --> 00:17:03.320
And so the big thing there

384
00:17:03.320 --> 00:17:07.260
is once you have the bigger picture, the purpose,

385
00:17:07.260 --> 00:17:08.540
and once you have the clarity,

386
00:17:08.540 --> 00:17:10.090
which is what I call the coaching,

387
00:17:10.090 --> 00:17:13.350
the path, the manual, the sort of map,

388
00:17:13.350 --> 00:17:17.190
then you can execute the workout properly.

389
00:17:17.190 --> 00:17:19.700
You can execute your training without wondering,

390
00:17:19.700 --> 00:17:20.750
why am I doing this?

391
00:17:20.750 --> 00:17:21.830
How is this gonna help me?

392
00:17:21.830 --> 00:17:23.350
Is this keeping me on my path

393
00:17:23.350 --> 00:17:25.090
towards my desired outcome?

394
00:17:25.090 --> 00:17:28.610
And is this what the coach and I discussed?

395
00:17:28.610 --> 00:17:30.380
It's all been laid out already.

396
00:17:30.380 --> 00:17:31.730
And we know that from swimming,

397
00:17:31.730 --> 00:17:33.800
we're just so ingrained in this

398
00:17:33.800 --> 00:17:36.360
that we don't, well, of course these 400 IMs

399
00:17:36.360 --> 00:17:38.680
are helping me swim my 400 IM better.

400
00:17:38.680 --> 00:17:40.860
Of course, this set of 200s

401
00:17:40.860 --> 00:17:43.370
with the middle hundred fly is helping me swim

402
00:17:43.370 --> 00:17:44.650
my 400 IM better.

403
00:17:44.650 --> 00:17:46.880
But in the endurance training world

404
00:17:46.880 --> 00:17:48.480
or in just in the work world,

405
00:17:48.480 --> 00:17:50.400
if you don't know where you're heading

406
00:17:50.400 --> 00:17:52.070
and why you're doing it,

407
00:17:52.070 --> 00:17:56.710
the quality of your work is always going to be limited

408
00:17:56.710 --> 00:18:00.400
because you're just constantly wasting cognitive energy,

409
00:18:00.400 --> 00:18:02.350
cognitive load as they call it,

410
00:18:02.350 --> 00:18:05.600
on other things in order to make it more intentional

411
00:18:05.600 --> 00:18:06.433
and clear for you.

412
00:18:06.433 --> 00:18:08.566
Once you have that out, you can hit flow.

413
00:18:08.566 --> 00:18:11.680
You're right in the moment because you're not worried

414
00:18:11.680 --> 00:18:13.060
about all the other things

415
00:18:13.060 --> 00:18:14.970
'cause they've been clarified for you.

416
00:18:14.970 --> 00:18:17.670
The scaffolding is set.

417
00:18:17.670 --> 00:18:19.960
And what I mean by that is when we start training,

418
00:18:19.960 --> 00:18:21.510
especially as masters athletes,

419
00:18:21.510 --> 00:18:22.410
not when we're younger,

420
00:18:22.410 --> 00:18:25.870
but as, the training is a scaffolding.

421
00:18:25.870 --> 00:18:28.700
What happens inside that scaffolding

422
00:18:28.700 --> 00:18:30.530
is unique to everybody.

