as well as the self-belief needed

787
00:31:17.530 --> 00:31:19.900
to set audacious goals.

788
00:31:19.900 --> 00:31:23.290
And in a display of vulnerability,

789
00:31:23.290 --> 00:31:27.610
how healing her past trauma taught her to thrive

790
00:31:27.610 --> 00:31:30.510
and find the joy in the journey.

791
00:31:30.510 --> 00:31:33.513
Here's a powerful clip from that conversation.

792
00:31:34.800 --> 00:31:37.210
So much of your life was premised

793
00:31:37.210 --> 00:31:40.190
on differentiating yourself from your mom,

794
00:31:40.190 --> 00:31:44.410
like out of a fear that you might follow in her footsteps

795
00:31:44.410 --> 00:31:45.330
in a certain way.

796
00:31:45.330 --> 00:31:48.190
And I would imagine that you felt

797
00:31:48.190 --> 00:31:51.680
like you had escaped that in some way,

798
00:31:51.680 --> 00:31:56.180
but as the op doc shows,

799
00:31:56.180 --> 00:31:58.010
and as you talk about in your book,

800
00:31:58.010 --> 00:32:01.620
like, nonetheless, you have this experience with depression

