2081
01:26:31.830 --> 01:26:33.660
about protein, meeting your protein needs

2082
01:26:33.660 --> 01:26:34.550
on a plant-based diet

2083
01:26:34.550 --> 01:26:35.950
so I don't wanna belabor the point,

2084
01:26:35.950 --> 01:26:37.475
but I haven't had you here to do it.

2085
01:26:37.475 --> 01:26:42.475
And you being a very strong physical specimen,

2086
01:26:42.670 --> 01:26:46.010
I think it's worthy if somebody's tuning into this

2087
01:26:46.010 --> 01:26:47.830
and isn't familiar with either of us

2088
01:26:47.830 --> 01:26:49.930
and perhaps this is their first introduction

2089
01:26:49.930 --> 01:26:52.090
to some of the ideas we're talking about

2090
01:26:52.090 --> 01:26:53.350
to at least spend a couple minutes

2091
01:26:53.350 --> 01:26:56.030
talking about the big protein question.

2092
01:26:56.030 --> 01:26:59.630
Because it still propagates, in terms of people

2093
01:26:59.630 --> 01:27:01.700
who are interested in moving towards

2094
01:27:01.700 --> 01:27:04.070
a more plant-centric diet but are fearful

2095
01:27:04.070 --> 01:27:06.950
of what that implies in terms of meeting

2096
01:27:06.950 --> 01:27:07.850
their protein needs,

2097
01:27:07.850 --> 01:27:12.433
especially for the active people amongst that cohort.

2098
01:27:13.680 --> 01:27:18.680
Yeah, so this was a very large fear of mine (chuckles)

2099
01:27:18.850 --> 01:27:22.150
when I was initially making the changes to my diet.

2100
01:27:22.150 --> 01:27:24.750
And I always remind myself of that

2101
01:27:24.750 --> 01:27:27.580
because it's easy to kinda dismiss it

2102
01:27:27.580 --> 01:27:32.330
and forget that, you know,

2103
01:27:32.330 --> 01:27:34.830
the sort of general school of thought

2104
01:27:34.830 --> 01:27:37.470
is that you get your protein from animal foods

2105
01:27:37.470 --> 01:27:39.550
and that plants are missing protein.

2106
01:27:39.550 --> 01:27:41.080
And to this day,

2107
01:27:41.080 --> 01:27:43.900
when you go to a restaurant or you go to Chipotle,

2108
01:27:43.900 --> 01:27:46.827
they say, "What protein do you want on this?"

2109
01:27:47.760 --> 01:27:52.293
And yeah, very rarely does that include plant protein.

2110
01:27:53.850 --> 01:27:55.950
Although that's, you know, it's starting to change.

2111
01:27:55.950 --> 01:27:57.010
I think the food environment's

2112
01:27:57.010 --> 01:28:00.360
starting to modify-
Definitely.

2113
01:28:00.360 --> 01:28:04.930
and we're seeing increases in plant protein options.

2114
01:28:04.930 --> 01:28:07.140
And I was chatting with Paul Shapiro

2115
01:28:08.480 --> 01:28:10.853
couple weeks ago now, and he's doing exciting things

2116
01:28:10.853 --> 01:28:12.031
with mycoprotein.
Yeah, it's pretty wild

2117
01:28:12.031 --> 01:28:15.063
what his company is doing right now with mushrooms.

2118
01:28:16.030 --> 01:28:16.930
Yeah. It's crazy.

2119
01:28:16.930 --> 01:28:20.460
You know, feeding these fungi microbes,

2120
01:28:20.460 --> 01:28:23.160
potato and sorghum,

2121
01:28:23.160 --> 01:28:27.570
and then producing this super protein-rich food.

2122
01:28:27.570 --> 01:28:30.430
I tried some as well and it's incredible.

2123
01:28:30.430 --> 01:28:32.780
I haven't tried it yet.

2124
01:28:32.780 --> 01:28:36.143
You know, that's certainly the future of food.

2125
01:28:37.370 --> 01:28:40.720
But overall I think there are

2126
01:28:40.720 --> 01:28:42.700
a few aspects of protein

2127
01:28:42.700 --> 01:28:45.393
that are somewhat misunderstood.

2128
01:28:46.440 --> 01:28:50.053
And we can perhaps clear up some of that confusion.

2129
01:28:51.200 --> 01:28:53.960
The first would be that plant protein

2130
01:28:53.960 --> 01:28:57.820
is missing certain essential amino acids.

2131
01:28:57.820 --> 01:29:01.860
And protein is made up of amino acids.

2132
01:29:01.860 --> 01:29:04.090
They're the little building blocks

2133
01:29:05.368 --> 01:29:08.780
and our body can make 11 of them

2134
01:29:08.780 --> 01:29:11.960
and the other nine are considered essential amino acids.

2135
01:29:11.960 --> 01:29:14.390
We have to get them through our food.

2136
01:29:14.390 --> 01:29:19.250
And the idea for many decades

2137
01:29:19.250 --> 01:29:21.400
has been that plants are missing

2138
01:29:21.400 --> 01:29:23.023
some of those amino acids.

2139
01:29:24.400 --> 01:29:28.170
And you hear this idea of complete protein, right?

2140
01:29:28.170 --> 01:29:33.170
And often people speak to quinoa and soy.

2141
01:29:33.440 --> 01:29:37.450
And I think definition here is really important.

2142
01:29:37.450 --> 01:29:39.080
It's critical to this.

2143
01:29:39.080 --> 01:29:40.830
Because I think there's a misunderstanding

2144
01:29:40.830 --> 01:29:43.090
of what complete protein means.

2145
01:29:43.090 --> 01:29:44.770
I think most people think,

2146
01:29:44.770 --> 01:29:47.880
okay, well, if quinoa and soy are complete proteins,

2147
01:29:47.880 --> 01:29:50.450
that means that these other plants

2148
01:29:50.450 --> 01:29:52.080
are missing amino acids.

2149
01:29:52.080 --> 01:29:53.340
They're inferior.

2150
01:29:53.340 --> 01:29:56.690
Yeah, or that they're just totally missing something

2151
01:29:56.690 --> 01:29:58.440
and that's not true.

2152
01:29:58.440 --> 01:30:02.850
So all plants contain all nine essential amino acids.

2153
01:30:02.850 --> 01:30:04.660
They're not missing.

2154
01:30:04.660 --> 01:30:06.570
There just are some of those plants

2155
01:30:06.570 --> 01:30:10.150
where certain amino acids are in lower amounts.

2156
01:30:10.150 --> 01:30:13.700
And so the definition of incomplete

2157
01:30:13.700 --> 01:30:16.170
actually by definition within the science,

2158
01:30:16.170 --> 01:30:19.840
although it's not used this way in general conversation,

2159
01:30:19.840 --> 01:30:22.740
is not that an amino acid is missing,

2160
01:30:22.740 --> 01:30:27.570
it's just that it is in a smaller percentage.

2161
01:30:27.570 --> 01:30:31.370
And if you were to eat only that food

2162
01:30:31.370 --> 01:30:33.050
for all of your calories,

2163
01:30:33.050 --> 01:30:35.140
then you might run into some trouble.

2164
01:30:35.140 --> 01:30:36.525
You might not consume enough

2165
01:30:36.525 --> 01:30:39.010
of a certain amino acid

2166
01:30:39.010 --> 01:30:42.020
to meet your body's daily requirement.

2167
01:30:42.020 --> 01:30:44.120
So you can imagine

2168
01:30:44.120 --> 01:30:47.090
that that's kind of a useful definition

2169
01:30:47.090 --> 01:30:49.130
for developing countries,

2170
01:30:49.130 --> 01:30:52.740
places where there is food security problems.

2171
01:30:52.740 --> 01:30:56.510
And if someone's living on one or two foods,

2172
01:30:56.510 --> 01:30:57.960
then that's important.

2173
01:30:57.960 --> 01:31:01.400
But if you're eating a diet where you have a range

2174
01:31:01.400 --> 01:31:03.770
of an abundance of food options,

2175
01:31:03.770 --> 01:31:07.030
then really it's not that helpful.

2176
01:31:07.030 --> 01:31:10.670
And so if you are eating

2177
01:31:10.670 --> 01:31:13.450
with diversity, you will,

2178
01:31:13.450 --> 01:31:15.423
you might be consuming for example,

2179
01:31:16.310 --> 01:31:19.100
grains that are low in lysine.

2180
01:31:19.100 --> 01:31:20.230
And look, it's true.

2181
01:31:20.230 --> 01:31:23.340
If you were to eat certain grains

2182
01:31:23.340 --> 01:31:24.260
and that was providing

2183
01:31:24.260 --> 01:31:26.880
your 3000, two thousand and a half thousand calories,

2184
01:31:26.880 --> 01:31:29.750
then you might fall short on lysine.

2185
01:31:29.750 --> 01:31:33.100
And the same could be said about certain beans.

2186
01:31:33.100 --> 01:31:36.040
If you eat a certain bean for all of your calories,

2187
01:31:36.040 --> 01:31:38.190
you might fall short on the thiamine.

2188
01:31:38.190 --> 01:31:40.800
But beans are very rich in lysine.

2189
01:31:40.800 --> 01:31:44.440
And when you start adding all these foods into your diet,

2190
01:31:44.440 --> 01:31:46.330
some might be low in a certain amino acid,

2191
01:31:46.330 --> 01:31:48.110
but the other food is really high.

2192
01:31:48.110 --> 01:31:50.100
Right, it's really an academic exercise

2193
01:31:50.100 --> 01:31:52.350
because almost no one is only eating one food.

2194
01:31:52.350 --> 01:31:53.300
Correct.
Unless you're like

2195
01:31:53.300 --> 01:31:54.380
the Spud Fit guy,

2196
01:31:54.380 --> 01:31:56.240
who's eating just potatoes for a year.

2197
01:31:56.240 --> 01:31:58.210
Or you are in a developing country

2198
01:31:58.210 --> 01:32:01.380
and there is a legitimate food scarcity issue.

2199
01:32:01.380 --> 01:32:02.725
But almost everybody is eating

2200
01:32:02.725 --> 01:32:05.820
at least two, three, five,

2201
01:32:05.820 --> 01:32:09.100
six, seven, 10 different foods

2202
01:32:09.100 --> 01:32:11.580
throughout the course of a day or two.

2203
01:32:11.580 --> 01:32:12.830
And if you're doing that,

2204
01:32:12.830 --> 01:32:14.060
you're rating with that diversity

2205
01:32:14.060 --> 01:32:16.110
and you're eating enough calories,

2206
01:32:16.110 --> 01:32:18.220
you will not run into problems.

2207
01:32:18.220 --> 01:32:20.943
You will get all of the essential amino acids

2208
01:32:20.943 --> 01:32:22.420
that your body needs.

2209
01:32:22.420 --> 01:32:25.270
And anyone can run a simple exercise.

2210
01:32:25.270 --> 01:32:28.100
Don't believe me. Download the Cronometer app.

2211
01:32:28.100 --> 01:32:29.690
It's a free app.

2212
01:32:29.690 --> 01:32:32.020
Plug in a day of eating

2213
01:32:32.020 --> 01:32:36.040
and you will quickly see that you will exceed

2214
01:32:36.040 --> 01:32:38.600
the hundred percent recommended amount

2215
01:32:38.600 --> 01:32:41.170
for all nine essential amino acids.

2216
01:32:41.170 --> 01:32:45.830
And you'll see, it's very hard not to exceed. (chuckles)

2217
01:32:45.830 --> 01:32:47.780
It would be more challenging to fall short on them

2218
01:32:47.780 --> 01:32:51.080
than it would be to consume enough of them.

2219
01:32:51.080 --> 01:32:53.470
All right, people of Podcastlandia, we did it.

2220
01:32:53.470 --> 01:32:54.540
This is the end.

2221
01:32:54.540 --> 01:32:57.490
And to put a cap on part one of this year's recap

2222
01:32:57.490 --> 01:33:00.850
is none other than planetary change agent

2223
01:33:00.850 --> 01:33:02.600
and entrepreneur, Paul Hawkin,

2224
01:33:02.600 --> 01:33:05.560
who joined me back on episode 627

2225
01:33:05.560 --> 01:33:07.657
to share his beautiful new book,

2226
01:33:07.657 --> 01:33:11.820
"Regeneration: Ending the Climate Crisis in One Generation".

2227
01:33:11.820 --> 01:33:15.950
Paul is someone who has indelibly shaped my perspective

2228
01:33:15.950 --> 01:33:20.080
and my actions when it comes to ecological responsibility.

2229
01:33:20.080 --> 01:33:22.920
And it's just an honor to close things out

2230
01:33:22.920 --> 01:33:24.693
with his words today.

2231
01:33:26.770 --> 01:33:29.730
The root cause of global warming

2232
01:33:29.730 --> 01:33:32.560
is a massive disconnections

2233
01:33:32.560 --> 01:33:34.470
between each other, between people,

2234
01:33:34.470 --> 01:33:36.500
between people and nature,

2235
01:33:36.500 --> 01:33:41.140
and nature itself, which is caused by humans,

2236
01:33:41.140 --> 01:33:43.370
habitat fragmentation, pollution,

2237
01:33:43.370 --> 01:33:47.263
acidification of the oceans, and onwards.

2238
01:33:49.781 --> 01:33:52.198
So regenerating and reversing

2239
01:33:54.420 --> 01:33:59.280
the climate crisis is really about reconnecting

2240
01:33:59.280 --> 01:34:00.603
those broken strands.

2241
01:34:01.490 --> 01:34:04.830
And that's what the solutions really are

2242
01:34:04.830 --> 01:34:07.520
as opposed to sort of standalone techniques

2243
01:34:07.520 --> 01:34:10.390
or technologies that's going to fix it.

2244
01:34:10.390 --> 01:34:13.230
That word fix doesn't even belong in the conversation

2245
01:34:13.230 --> 01:34:16.110
because it's not an it, and you can't fix it.

2246
01:34:16.110 --> 01:34:18.520
The atmosphere is the biosphere.

2247
01:34:18.520 --> 01:34:23.040
It does the same thing and we are part of it.

2248
01:34:23.040 --> 01:34:26.160
And nature never makes a mistake, only we do.

2249
01:34:26.160 --> 01:34:28.260
So let's look at what we're doing.

2250
01:34:28.260 --> 01:34:31.620
And regeneration is very much about alignment

2251
01:34:31.620 --> 01:34:33.530
with the living world,

2252
01:34:33.530 --> 01:34:37.350
with the way it works and always has.

2253
01:34:37.350 --> 01:34:40.003
And so, as you said,

2254
01:34:40.840 --> 01:34:45.130
what we've done conversationally and sort of declaratively

2255
01:34:45.130 --> 01:34:47.250
and almost imperatively

2256
01:34:47.250 --> 01:34:49.180
is individuate the problem,

2257
01:34:49.180 --> 01:34:53.070
which is this is what you can do or should do.

2258
01:34:53.070 --> 01:34:56.570
And it's true, those are good things.

2259
01:34:56.570 --> 01:34:58.700
You know, recycling and use cold water

2260
01:34:58.700 --> 01:34:59.800
in your washing machine,

2261
01:34:59.800 --> 01:35:04.020
and try not to, drive an EV if you can afford it,

2262
01:35:04.020 --> 01:35:05.520
et cetera, et cetera.

2263
01:35:05.520 --> 01:35:08.380
But I think people understand

2264
01:35:08.380 --> 01:35:11.240
that even if they do them,

2265
01:35:11.240 --> 01:35:13.700
they know it's not sufficient

2266
01:35:13.700 --> 01:35:15.330
to the task at hand.

2267
01:35:15.330 --> 01:35:17.670
And so it actually makes people more disempowered

2268
01:35:17.670 --> 01:35:18.503
in a funny way,

2269
01:35:18.503 --> 01:35:20.170
even though they're actually participating

2270
01:35:20.170 --> 01:35:22.170
in their kind of token way.

2271
01:35:22.170 --> 01:35:26.540
And then they look to governments,

2272
01:35:26.540 --> 01:35:28.880
they look to the Conference of the Parties,

2273
01:35:28.880 --> 01:35:30.660
the UN Framework on Climate Change.

2274
01:35:30.660 --> 01:35:33.670
They look for these annual meetings,

2275
01:35:33.670 --> 01:35:35.423
there's one in Glasgow in November,

2276
01:35:36.340 --> 01:35:37.830
for something to happen.

2277
01:35:37.830 --> 01:35:40.780
Like hoping that politicians

2278
01:35:40.780 --> 01:35:42.360
will get together and solve the problem.

2279
01:35:42.360 --> 01:35:45.170
If politicians knew what to do,

2280
01:35:45.170 --> 01:35:47.130
we wouldn't be in the situation we are today.

2281
01:35:47.130 --> 01:35:48.360
And that's just not gonna happen.

2282
01:35:48.360 --> 01:35:50.960
Not to say we can't say it, but you know.

2283
01:35:50.960 --> 01:35:53.470
So then you feel like there's this gulf

2284
01:35:53.470 --> 01:35:58.340
between these huge meta-institutions,

2285
01:35:58.340 --> 01:35:59.690
corporations and governments,

2286
01:35:59.690 --> 01:36:01.100
and then you as an individual.

2287
01:36:01.100 --> 01:36:02.630
And that's what, again, what "Regeneration"

2288
01:36:02.630 --> 01:36:03.463
is trying to say.

2289
01:36:03.463 --> 01:36:05.040
Whoa, wait a minute.

2290
01:36:05.040 --> 01:36:08.689
That's not where the solution is gonna come from,

2291
01:36:08.689 --> 01:36:09.583
you know.
Right.

2292
01:36:10.697 --> 01:36:15.650
"Regeneration" is sort of bedfellows

2293
01:36:15.650 --> 01:36:18.310
with this idea of symbiosis.

2294
01:36:18.310 --> 01:36:20.680
Like how can we live more symbiotically on the planet?

2295
01:36:20.680 --> 01:36:24.340
And understanding that and really embodying that

2296
01:36:24.340 --> 01:36:28.400
begins with really fully embracing

2297
01:36:28.400 --> 01:36:32.830
and acknowledging that we are all

2298
01:36:32.830 --> 01:36:35.390
microsystems that are a part of a macrosystem.

2299
01:36:35.390 --> 01:36:37.670
And it's sort of belying the idea

2300
01:36:37.670 --> 01:36:39.760
that nature's over there and we're over here

2301
01:36:39.760 --> 01:36:42.460
and we venture into nature and out of nature.

2302
01:36:42.460 --> 01:36:45.500
And yet fundamentally that's just a falsehood

2303
01:36:45.500 --> 01:36:47.270
because the cells in our body

2304
01:36:47.270 --> 01:36:48.700
and everything that we're made up of

2305
01:36:48.700 --> 01:36:52.160
is of course part and parcel of this environment.

2306
01:36:52.160 --> 01:36:55.503
And in terms of the solution, once you acknowledge that,

2307
01:36:56.480 --> 01:36:57.980
I think what you begin to understand

2308
01:36:57.980 --> 01:37:02.720
and what the book kind of does a beautiful job conveying

2309
01:37:02.720 --> 01:37:04.740
is the idea

2310
01:37:07.601 --> 01:37:09.250
that there's this...

2311
01:37:10.130 --> 01:37:11.600
The problem is systemic,

2312
01:37:11.600 --> 01:37:14.330
that we can't truly move

2313
01:37:14.330 --> 01:37:18.240
into this more symbiotic regenerative relationship

2314
01:37:18.240 --> 01:37:22.590
with the planet until we have some corrective measures

2315
01:37:22.590 --> 01:37:23.860
with our systems at large, right?

2316
01:37:23.860 --> 01:37:26.580
There's this gigantic misalignment of incentives

2317
01:37:26.580 --> 01:37:31.210
across the board, be it by dint of governmental bodies

2318
01:37:31.210 --> 01:37:34.370
or the tectonic plates of capitalism,

2319
01:37:34.370 --> 01:37:36.400
all of these forces that the individual

2320
01:37:36.400 --> 01:37:41.000
feels powerless to have any control over or say over

2321
01:37:42.010 --> 01:37:43.970
that perpetuate the problem.

2322
01:37:43.970 --> 01:37:46.520
So short of revolution,

2323
01:37:46.520 --> 01:37:49.480
like how are we creating better incentives

2324
01:37:49.480 --> 01:37:51.200
for the systems that are in play?

2325
01:37:51.200 --> 01:37:54.690
Or how do we create better systems with incentives

2326
01:37:54.690 --> 01:37:57.823
that could supplant the systems that are leading us astray?

2327
01:37:59.070 --> 01:38:00.787
That is the question.

2328
01:38:00.787 --> 01:38:02.310
And I think that

2329
01:38:04.380 --> 01:38:08.420
between the individual and meta-institutions,

2330
01:38:08.420 --> 01:38:13.420
global institutions, is something else called agency.

2331
01:38:14.100 --> 01:38:17.523
And agency is sort of been overlooked.

2332
01:38:19.070 --> 01:38:21.520
There is no such thing as an individual.

2333
01:38:21.520 --> 01:38:23.880
That's sort of a delusion

2334
01:38:23.880 --> 01:38:27.093
we wake up with in the morning. (laughing)

2335
01:38:28.720 --> 01:38:30.650
But functionally, there's no such thing.

2336
01:38:30.650 --> 01:38:33.340
And every person has agency.

2337
01:38:33.340 --> 01:38:35.720
It's their family, it's their friends, it's their community,

2338
01:38:35.720 --> 01:38:36.553
it's their neighborhood,

2339
01:38:36.553 --> 01:38:37.695
it's their church, it's their synagogue,

2340
01:38:37.695 --> 01:38:40.000
it's a school, it's where they teach,

2341
01:38:40.000 --> 01:38:43.590
it's their city, it's their company, colleagues.

2342
01:38:43.590 --> 01:38:44.900
It goes on and on and on.

2343
01:38:44.900 --> 01:38:47.460
And we have a network.

2344
01:38:47.460 --> 01:38:49.090
We're all part of networks

2345
01:38:49.090 --> 01:38:52.330
and that is where we have influence

2346
01:38:52.330 --> 01:38:54.710
and where we can make a difference.

2347
01:38:54.710 --> 01:38:59.560
And the, I think a lot of people have felt

2348
01:38:59.560 --> 01:39:03.870
or come to think that if we get renewables right

2349
01:39:03.870 --> 01:39:07.920
or we do this, we do that, that again, we'll fix it.

2350
01:39:07.920 --> 01:39:12.580
But like there's some Archimedean solution.

2351
01:39:12.580 --> 01:39:14.540
If we pull hard enough,

2352
01:39:14.540 --> 01:39:15.700
the problem is gonna go away.

2353
01:39:15.700 --> 01:39:16.533
Right.

2354
01:39:16.533 --> 01:39:19.630
And rather than understanding that the solution

2355
01:39:19.630 --> 01:39:22.960
is everywhere, it's ubiquitous, it's local,

2356
01:39:22.960 --> 01:39:27.510
regional, it's where agency exists

2357
01:39:27.510 --> 01:39:31.080
and that is everywhere on earth with every culture,

2358
01:39:31.080 --> 01:39:35.420
every society, and every country.

2359
01:39:35.420 --> 01:39:37.970
And so that's the good news,

2360
01:39:37.970 --> 01:39:42.350
which is that we can solve this.

2361
01:39:42.350 --> 01:39:43.510
We really can.

2362
01:39:43.510 --> 01:39:44.640
But we can't solve it

2363
01:39:44.640 --> 01:39:47.500
if we think someone's gonna solve it for us.

2364
01:39:47.500 --> 01:39:50.990
Or if we come to believe that individuals

2365
01:39:50.990 --> 01:39:53.340
are to blame and that they're responsible

2366
01:39:53.340 --> 01:39:54.173
and they'll solve it.

2367
01:39:54.173 --> 01:39:55.860
We kinda know that one's not true.

2368
01:39:55.860 --> 01:39:57.050
Right.

2369
01:39:57.050 --> 01:39:59.820
I'm not saying we don't have personal responsibility.

2370
01:39:59.820 --> 01:40:00.653
Of course we do.

2371
01:40:00.653 --> 01:40:04.150
But that that alone is going to be sufficient.

2372
01:40:04.150 --> 01:40:07.430
And so when we look at the institutions

2373
01:40:07.430 --> 01:40:10.440
and with the perverse incentives that they have,

2374
01:40:10.440 --> 01:40:13.140
the economic institutions, the political institutions,

2375
01:40:15.130 --> 01:40:18.150
they are all extractive.

2376
01:40:18.150 --> 01:40:21.370
That is to say every institution that we've come to know

2377
01:40:21.370 --> 01:40:25.440
and trust or not trust, but buy from, or believe in,

2378
01:40:25.440 --> 01:40:29.210
or invest in, or own shares in is extractive.

2379
01:40:29.210 --> 01:40:31.920
You know, it's just taking life.

2380
01:40:31.920 --> 01:40:34.490
And we sorta take that for granted that.

2381
01:40:34.490 --> 01:40:37.880
You know, well, don't make a mess. (chuckles)

2382
01:40:37.880 --> 01:40:38.713
You know.

2383
01:40:38.713 --> 01:40:40.407
Or clean up your mess, that kind of thing.

2384
01:40:40.407 --> 01:40:42.910
And that's sustainability in a way.

2385
01:40:42.910 --> 01:40:44.930
But extraction is taking life

2386
01:40:44.930 --> 01:40:47.090
and when you take life, that's degeneration.

2387
01:40:47.090 --> 01:40:50.240
That's what degeneration is when you take life.

2388
01:40:50.240 --> 01:40:55.240
And so "Regeneration" is really

2389
01:40:55.520 --> 01:40:56.980
not about blaming

2390
01:40:56.980 --> 01:41:00.147
and sort of demonizing

2391
01:41:03.020 --> 01:41:06.710
those institutions or those economic sectors so much

2392
01:41:06.710 --> 01:41:09.280
as saying wait, that road,

2393
01:41:09.280 --> 01:41:12.330
that degeneration road, doesn't go much further.

2394
01:41:12.330 --> 01:41:15.600
Everything's screaming at us, all the science,

2395
01:41:15.600 --> 01:41:17.070
our experiences, and so forth.

2396
01:41:17.070 --> 01:41:18.780
Like that road doesn't go much further.

2397
01:41:18.780 --> 01:41:20.560
Why are we going down that road?

2398
01:41:20.560 --> 01:41:22.870
And so "Regeneration" is about a 180 pivot.

2399
01:41:22.870 --> 01:41:26.250
Like, can we just stop and go the other way?

2400
01:41:26.250 --> 01:41:29.280
Can we not regenerate the world

2401
01:41:29.280 --> 01:41:32.080
and have a GDP and an economy and jobs

2402
01:41:32.080 --> 01:41:34.040
rather than degenerate it?

2403
01:41:34.040 --> 01:41:36.510
And the fact is we can,

2404
01:41:36.510 --> 01:41:39.160
and it's really a question of healing the future

2405
01:41:39.160 --> 01:41:40.090
or stealing the future.

2406
01:41:40.090 --> 01:41:42.660
'Cause what we're doing is stealing the future.

2407
01:41:42.660 --> 01:41:44.500
Now, it used to be from our children,

2408
01:41:44.500 --> 01:41:46.740
now it's from ourselves practically.

2409
01:41:46.740 --> 01:41:50.120
And so it really isn't like

2410
01:41:52.296 --> 01:41:55.800
I could say something that what's happening

2411
01:41:55.800 --> 01:41:57.770
with respect to climate is wrong or...

2412
01:41:57.770 --> 01:41:59.090
Not at all. It's all great.

2413
01:41:59.090 --> 01:42:01.420
What everybody's doing is fantastic.

2414
01:42:01.420 --> 01:42:03.510
But unless we actually do address

2415
01:42:03.510 --> 01:42:07.390
those institutional incentives,

2416
01:42:07.390 --> 01:42:10.540
and actually assumptions that are so deep

2417
01:42:10.540 --> 01:42:13.240
that people don't even understand them as assumptions,

2418
01:42:14.934 --> 01:42:17.851
then we won't have a chance at all.

2419
01:42:19.410 --> 01:42:21.770
Because the, and you know, Rich,

2420
01:42:21.770 --> 01:42:23.313
one of the things too,

2421
01:42:24.820 --> 01:42:26.250
go back to the fix it thing.

2422
01:42:26.250 --> 01:42:28.430
Like, you know Bill Gates and others,

2423
01:42:28.430 --> 01:42:30.350
like John Kerry, for example, are saying,

2424
01:42:30.350 --> 01:42:33.500
if we don't do nuclear, we're screwed, okay? (laughing)

2425
01:42:33.500 --> 01:42:38.300
And this idea that there is this one thing.

2426
01:42:38.300 --> 01:42:41.660
But you could have renewable energy

2427
01:42:41.660 --> 01:42:43.870
or nuclear energy for the whole world today

2428
01:42:45.330 --> 01:42:47.220
and we'd still be going right over the cliff

2429
01:42:47.220 --> 01:42:49.980
because we're destroying all the living systems on earth.

2430
01:42:49.980 --> 01:42:52.360
We're destroying our oceans, our fisheries, our land,

2431
01:42:52.360 --> 01:42:56.140
our forest, our insects, our pollinators, and so forth.

2432
01:42:56.140 --> 01:42:57.580
That has nothing to do with renewable energy

2433
01:42:57.580 --> 01:42:58.720
or fossil fuel energy.

2434
01:42:58.720 --> 01:43:00.570
That has to do with us.

2435
01:43:00.570 --> 01:43:02.630
And so we have to see it, as you said earlier,

2436
01:43:02.630 --> 01:43:04.100
as a system, it's whole.

2437
01:43:04.100 --> 01:43:06.953
You can't silo it and separate it out

2438
01:43:07.999 --> 01:43:10.180
and say we're gonna do that and do this and do that.

2439
01:43:10.180 --> 01:43:11.900
You can do that,

2440
01:43:11.900 --> 01:43:15.510
but unless you step back and look at it systemically,

2441
01:43:15.510 --> 01:43:18.940
you're not gonna get to the core cause or core cure.

2442
01:43:18.940 --> 01:43:20.880
What an incredible year.

2443
01:43:20.880 --> 01:43:22.810
Thank you for joining me today.

2444
